{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>One bull.</b> One ram from here and one ram from here, and a bull in the middle. And why three? Corresponding to the three patriarchs. The bull corresponds to Abraham, as it is written: ״ואל הבקר רץ אברהם״. The rams correspond to Isaac and Jacob. And unleavened bread — corresponding to Hagar and Sarah, for Abraham said to them: ״מהרי שלש סאין״ — three species corresponding to three se'ahs. And further on it is written ״וחלת לחם״ — on account of the offerings the bread is blessed, as Rav Huna bar Abba said: at the time when they would offer the offerings, a person would take a se'ah of wheat to the mill, and when they would bring from it a se'ah of fine flour, a se'ah of meal, a se'ah of bran; but now one takes out only a se'ah and a bit more. And in the merit of the libations the wines are blessed. And there was an incident involving a certain student who went outside Jerusalem; they recognized him as a student and said to him: Take three gold coins and stay with us, but he refused. He said to them: I have one vine that is dearer to me than anything you could give me, for it produces for me six hundred barrels of wine every year, and I sell them at high prices. And likewise, in the merit of the first fruits the fruits are blessed. And there was an incident involving Yonatan ben Elazar, who was sitting under a fig tree. Dew descended and the figs exuded honey until it reached the ground, and the wind would knead it with the dust; and a she-goat came and would drip milk, and the honey would mix with the milk. He said to his students: Come and I will show you a taste of the World to Come. These were nullified — all were nullified, as it is said: ״זרעתם הרבה והבא מעט״, ״אכול ולא לשבעה״, ״לבוש ולא לחום לו״. ״זרעתם הרבה והבא מעט״ — from when the meal-offerings were taken away. ״אכול ולא לשבעה״ — from when the showbread was taken away. ״שתו ולא לשכרה״ — from when the libations were taken away. ״לבוש ולא לחום לו״ — from when the priestly garments were taken away. There are no figs on the fig tree — from when the first fruits were taken away. ״גזר ממכלה צאן״ — from when the daily offerings were taken away. And there is no cattle in the stalls — from when the פרי החג was taken away. And in the future to come, the Holy One, blessed be He, will restore everything, as it is said: ״ואתם הרי ישראל ענפכם״ etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The word [כנגד] appears bracketed in the source; resolved as 'corresponding to.' פרי החג rendered literally; likely refers to the festival bull-offerings."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:23.801033170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}